      "bullets": [
        "Combining stack-based Forth and homoiconic Lisp simplifies self-hosting interpreters and metacompilation on resource-constrained embedded systems.",
        "Implementing Lisp on a Forth core provides dynamic, symbolic macro evaluation while retaining low-level memory access and micro-architecture control.",
        "Bidirectional language bootstrapping bridges stack-machine efficiency with functional dynamic execution for custom embedded virtual machine runtimes."
